Experiment 1.1: Contain duplicate (Leetcode Problem 217)

Aim: Given an integer array nums, return true if any value appears at least twice in the array, and return false if every element is distinct.

Algorithm:

1.)Start
2.)Take the input array nums.
3.)Sort the array in ascending order.
4.)Traverse the sorted array from the second element (i = 1) to the last element.
5.)For each element, compare it with its previous element:
      •If nums[i] == nums[i-1], a duplicate is found.
      •Return true.
6.)If the loop completes without finding any duplicate, return false.
7.)End

Code:

class Solution {
public:
    bool containsDuplicate(vector<int>& nums) {
        
        sort(nums.begin(),nums.end());
        for(int i=1;i<nums.size();i++){
            if(nums[i] == nums[i-1]){
                return true;
            }  
        }
        return false;
    }
};


Experiment 1.2: Contain Duplicate 2 (Leetcode Problem 219)

Aim: Given an integer array nums and an integer k, return true if there are two distinct indices i and j in the array such that nums[i] == nums[j] and abs(i - j) <= k.

Algorithm:

1.)Start
2.)Take the input array nums and integer k.
3.)Create an empty hash map mp to store each element and its latest index.
4.)Traverse the array from index 0 to n-1.
5.)For each element nums[i]:
   •Check if nums[i] already exists in the hash map.
    •If it exists:
        •Calculate the distance between the current index and the previous index: 
           i - mp[nums[i]].
    •If the distance is less than or equal to k, return true.
        •Update the hash map by storing the current index:
           mp[nums[i]] = i.
6.)If the loop finishes without finding such a pair, return false.
7.)End

Code:

class Solution {
public:
    bool containsNearbyDuplicate(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
            unordered_map<int,int>mp;
            for(int i=0;i<nums.size();i++){
                if(mp.find(nums[i])!=mp.end()){
                    if(i-mp[nums[i]]<=k){
                        return true;
                    }
                }
                mp[nums[i]]=i;
            }
            return false;
    }
};
